<!-- ── TRAVEL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="travel">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">Getting here</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Travel & <em>Stay</em></h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Ondo Town is a beautiful city in Ondo State, Nigeria. Here's everything you need to plan your trip.</p>
    <div class="travel-grid">
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🚗</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">From Lagos</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">Take the Sagamu–Ore Expressway via Ore. The drive is approximately 3–4 hours (240 km). Buses run from Ojota Motor Park. Interstate buses are also available.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">~3–4 hrs by road</div>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">✈️</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">From Abuja</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">Fly into Akure Airport (AKR) — the closest airport to Ondo Town (~45 min drive). Flights run frequently from Nnamdi Azikiwe International Airport.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">~1hr flight + 45min drive</div>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🏨</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">Esporta Suites Hotel & Resorts</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">One of Ondo Town's best-rated hotels — pool, restaurant & bar with live band evenings, DSTV, free parking and 24hr security. Rooms range from Standard to Royal Suite.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">₦45,000–₦105,000 / night · ~10 min from venue</div>
        <a class="btn-book" href="https://hotels.ng/hotel/45634-esporta-suites-hotel-resorts-ondo">Book Now</a>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🏨</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">Polak Hotels</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">A long-established hotel in the heart of Ondo Town with Deluxe rooms, Jacuzzi Super Deluxe rooms and Luxury Suites, plus a restaurant, gym, roof garden and airport shuttle on request.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">From ₦20,000 / night · ~5 min from venue</div>
        <a class="btn-book" href="tel:+2349069364017">Call to Book</a>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🏨</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">Citywalk Hotel</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">A modern hotel on Brigadier Ademulegun Road with an executive bar/restaurant, laundry service, 24-hour power supply and secure parking.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">Contact hotel for rates · ~5 min from venue</div>
        <a class="btn-book" href="tel:+2347053273700">Call to Book</a>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🏨</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">Labim Hotel & Event Centre</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">This is our Traditional Wedding venue itself, on Akure Road — a 3-star hotel with 16 rooms (family rooms available), each with AC, flat-screen TV and private bathroom, plus a restaurant, bar, terrace and free parking. Staying here puts you right at the celebration.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">Contact hotel for rates · Traditional Wedding venue</div>
        <a class="btn-book" href="tel:+2349035066145">Call to Book</a>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🏨</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">PK Continental Hotel & Suites</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">A modern 3-star hotel in the heart of Ondo City with 40 spacious, air-conditioned rooms, complimentary breakfast, free Wi-Fi, 32" cable TV, on-site restaurant/bar and 24hr front desk.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">Contact hotel for rates · Akinjagunla St, Ojojo Road, Ondo</div>
        <a class="btn-book" href="https://pkcontinentalhotel.com/">Book Now</a>
      </div>
      <div class="travel-card reveal">
        <div class="travel-card-icon">🏨</div>
        <div class="travel-card-title">Robertware Hotel & Suites</div>
        <p class="travel-card-text">A relaxed 23-room hotel with rainfall showers, an outdoor pool, banquet hall, complimentary English breakfast and free self parking — a comfortable, well-reviewed option in Ondo Town.</p>
        <div class="travel-card-sub">Contact hotel for rates · Robertware Drive, Akinyele St, Ondo</div>
        <a class="btn-book" href="https://www.facebook.com/robertwarehotel/">Book Now</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--light);margin-top:16px;text-align:center">Rates as of August 2026 and subject to change — please confirm directly with each hotel before booking.</p>
    <div class="map-wrap">
      <iframe src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=Labim+Hotel+and+Event+Centre,+Km+2+Akure+Road,+Ondo,+Nigeria&output=embed" width="100%" height="100%" style="border:0" allowfullscreen loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="faq">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-label">Need to know</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Common <em>Questions</em></h2>
    <div class="faq-list" id="faqList">
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">What is the dress code?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">For the Traditional Wedding, we encourage guests to wear <strong>Aso-Ebi</strong> or elegant traditional Nigerian attire. For the White Wedding, the dress code is <strong>formal or semi-formal</strong>. Details on Aso-Ebi fabric will be shared separately.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I bring children?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Children are warmly welcome! Please include them in your guest count when you RSVP so we can prepare adequately. We'll have a designated family-friendly area.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Is there parking available?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes, parking will be available at the venue. We also encourage car-pooling and will coordinate guest shuttles from key pickup points.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Will there be a live stream?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes! We know not everyone can make it in person, so we plan to live stream the White Wedding ceremony. Details on the streaming link will be shared closer to the date on our social media pages.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">What time should I arrive?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">We kindly ask all guests to arrive <strong>30–45 minutes before the ceremony start time</strong>. This gives us time to seat everyone before proceedings begin. Nigerian time is beautiful, but let's make an exception for this one! 😄</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">How do I confirm my RSVP?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Simply fill out the RSVP form above on this page. You'll receive a confirmation and your response will be saved. If you encounter any issues, please reach out to us directly.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

